    "q-57508": {
      "dom_id": "step-q57508",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A pizzeria charges $$15$ for a cheese pizza and $$3$ for each topping.\n\nWhat expression gives the total cost, in dollars, of a pizza with $n$ toppings?",
      "worked_solution": "If $n$ is the number of toppings, and the pizzeria charges $$3$ per topping, then the cost for $n$ toppings must be $3n.$ \n\nHowever, there is also a fixed fee for the cheese pizza. This fee is $$15.$ Consequently, the constant term of the expression should be $15.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of a pizza with $n$ toppings is:\n\n$$\n3n+15\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
