    "q-110281": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110281",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Mike is going to buy a baseball bat. The price of the bat is $P$ dollars, and Mike also has to pay a tax of $12%.$\n\nWhich expression represents the total cost of the bat, in dollars, after applying the tax?",
      "worked_solution": "The price of the bat before taxes is $P$ dollars. \n\nThe amount of tax Mike has to  pay is $12%$ of the price of the bat, or $0.12P.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the bat after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nP+0.12P\n$$",
