    "q-44808": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44808",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "A bouquet of flowers consists of $5$ roses and $4$ violets. The cost of one rose is $R$ dollars and the cost of one violet is $V$ dollars. Joseph is purchasing some bouquets for a graduation ceremony, and his total bill comes to $10(5R+4V)$ dollars.\n\nWhat does the factor $10$ mean in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "Five roses cost $5R$ dollars and four violets cost $4V$ dollars. Thus, the cost, in dollars, of a bouquet is\n\n$$\n5R+4V.\n$$\n\nJoseph's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n10(5R+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $10$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $10$ must be the total number of bouquets that Joseph purchased.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
