      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars. Kate is purchasing some pizzas and drinks for her family and the total bill comes to $6S+3M$ dollars. \n\nWhat does the factor $3$ mean in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars.\n\nKate's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n6S+3M.\n$$\n\nHence, the factor $3$ must be the total number of medium drinks that Kate purchased.",
