    "q-110316": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110316",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "A bouquet of flowers consists of $8$ tulips and $4$ violets. The cost of one tulip is $T$ dollars and  the cost of one violet is $V$ dollars. Thomas is purchasing some bouquets for a wedding, and his total bill comes to $12(8T+4V)$ dollars.\n\nWhat does the factor $12$ mean in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "Eight tulips cost $8T$ dollars, and four violets cost $4V$ dollars. Thus, the cost,  in dollars, of a bouquet is\n\n$$\n8T+4V.\n$$\n\nThomas' bill,  in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n12(8T+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $12$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $12$ must be the total number of bouquets that Thomas purchased.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
